WEBVTT

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.730
All right, the action is heating up!

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.640
This is the second match of the final round

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.170
of the Vanguard National Championship!

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:16.180
It's the end of the fifth turn 
and both players have 3 damage,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.100
which shows that this is indeed 
an evenly-matched fight!

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.570
It certainly is a wonderful, gripping 
r-<i>o</i>-ller coaster ride of a fight, isn't it?

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.570
Will AL4 continue their string of unbroken 
wins here and take the championship?

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:32.010
Or will Q4 avenge the loss of the first match

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.180
and force a play-off in the third match?!

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.140
In the end, which team will win?!

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.010
An evenly-matched fight, he says?

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.360
Poor, blind MC.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.990
Once he sees my next turn, he'll think again.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.320
This is the Pale Moon Circus,

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.150
and the much-awaited third act

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.310
will now begin!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.510
I ride Barking Manticore!

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.480
I activate its skill and 
draw one card from my deck.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.510
I put one card from my hand into the Soul.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.060
I call Nightmare Doll, Alice 
and Barking Cerberus!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.250
Cerberus, take out Amaterasu!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.310
I guard with Dream Eater!

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.120
With a boost from Turquoise... 
Manticore, attack Amaterasu!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.730
Crimson Beast Tamer is in the Soul,

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.060
so both units receive +3000,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.250
for a grand total of 22000 power!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.370
No guard...

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.600
Drive trigger...

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.940
First check.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.950
Second check.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.350
Critical trigger is activated!

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.080
I give the power to Alice and 
the extra critical to Manticore!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.270
Uh oh! That makes 5 damage!

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:46.960
Whatever you do, protect 
against the next attack!

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.470
You don't have to tell me that!

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.780
Lord of the Fight

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.030
With a boost from Skull Juggler...

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.250
Alice, attack Amaterasu!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.900
I guard with Battle Sister, Ginger and 
Goddess of the Crescent Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:15.420
Anyway, that's a relief!

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:18.280
No, you can't breathe easy yet.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.640
You understand, don't you?

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.840
You have 5 damage; I have 3.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:30.760
If you don't win on the next turn, 
your loss is all but assured.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.650
That's not for you to decide!

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.310
Oh, do you still have some spirit left?

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.050
I wonder how long you'll 
be able to hold on to it...

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.090
Along with the cold-blooded smile 
floating in the pale moonlight,

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.170
let's bring the curtain down!

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:47.930
Okay?

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.020
Draw!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.260
Amaterasu's Soulcharge!

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.620
I check the top card of my deck.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.780
I return it to the bottom of the deck.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.190
I call Oracle Guardian, Gemini and 
Goddess of the Crescent Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.800
With a boost from Gemini,

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.300
Oracle Guardian, Red Eye attacks Alice!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.560
She attacked the rear-guard again?!

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.790
ARGA, yo!

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:31.140
And not Cerberus, which can 
intercept, but Alice...

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.640
Come on! You have to win 
this turn, remember?!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.540
Misaki is doing it for the next turn...

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:42.320
Her strategy is picking off the rear-guard 
to cut down the number of attacks, right?

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.930
But just doing that won't...

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:48.220
That's right. You'll never be able 
to win just by protecting yourself.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.930
Whatever...

00:05:55.850 --> 00:06:00.190
Red Eye's skill is being able to 
Soulcharge when its attack hits.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.300
I don't want to let her get that 
eighth card into the Soul...

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:06.950
I need to...

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.960
Protect me, Dynamite Juggler!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.170
She guarded herself, like I figured.

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:20.400
But this is a superb fight.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.170
Yeah.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.030
I hate to admit it, but she really 
lives up to the Foo Fighter reputation.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.080
It'll be okay.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.740
I'm sure Misaki will win.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:38.050
She'll win and then pass it on to me.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:41.580
Brother...

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:46.270
Right! If anyone can do it, Misaki can!

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.320
With a boost from Goddess 
of the Crescent Moon,

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.200
Amaterasu attacks Manticore!

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.190
No guard.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:00.180
Drive trigger, first check.

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.880
Second check...

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:05.220
No trigger.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.010
Damage trigger check.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.610
No trigger.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.870
I attack Alice with Battle 
Maiden, Tagitsuhime!

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.380
I activate her skill! +3000 power!

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.340
Oh, dear. Are you that afraid of Alice?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.940
Even though she's such a cute doll...

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.600
Are you gonna guard or not?

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.940
No guard.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.730
Turn end.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:51.490
Whew! Now I can turn off the 
light when I go to sleep tonight!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.320
Huh?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.870
I mean, that giant doll is likely 
to show up in a dream, you know?!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.530
And that'd be really scary!

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.120
Huh...?

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.780
What's Lose-umi talking about, at his age?

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.540
LU is a total coward, yo!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.180
W-What was that?!

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:12.490
Well, it is a "Nightmare" 
doll, so he's not wrong.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.100
So she just got up to 4 damage this turn...

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.730
If Misaki takes even 1 more point 
of damage during the next turn...

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:20.600
Yeah...

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.970
Q4 will lose.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:26.670
Draw.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:33.720
It's been fun, but I have to raise the 
curtain for the finale of my Pale Moon Circus.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:37.820
Listen to the crack of the whip of 
the queen who can stir up a storm!

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.440
Come, Mistress Hurricane!

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:46.490
There are over eight cards in the 
Soul, so she receives +1000 power!

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:49.200
And then,

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.500
Hurricane's Counterblast!

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.240
Come back, Nightmare Doll Alice!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.790
S-S-She's back!!

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.370
Don't look this way!

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:11.370
With that, Deadly Shadow 
Beast can take place again...

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.410
Misaki...

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:17.610
An assassin never lets her quarry escape.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:23.130
With attacks like that, you'll 
never be able to evade

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:25.330
the deadly traps of the Pale Moon Circus!

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:31.700
So terrified you can't speak?

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.920
You've got a surprisingly cute side.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.490
Toshiki Kai...

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.390
So he did come...

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:49.960
Perhaps he can't face his teammates 
after disgracing himself.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.350
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.340
No trigger, huh?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.800
I win.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:26.470
I'm going to use this 
power to take everything.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.800
And nothing can stop me.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:30.910
<i>No one.</i>

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:36.420
Ren!

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.210
Pathetic...

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.000
Ren's already lost interest in Aichi Sendou,

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.890
and now his attachment to Kai will fade away.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.560
Then, finally, Ren will look at me...

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:59.350
And if I win here,

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.380
he'll favor me even more.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:05.710
I'll become Ren's most valuable fighter...

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:10.120
For that purpose, I'm going to take you down,

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.590
Misaki Tokura!

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.940
I call Midnight Bunny!

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.300
Alice's attack and Bunny's boost.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:43.780
If both of them succeed, this attack 
will have even more potential.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.660
These are my circus's proud star units.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.120
With a boost from Skull Juggler...

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:53.570
Alice, attack Amaterasu!

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.620
I guard with Lozenge Magus!

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:07.860
In any event, you're 
keeping up a steady guard.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.790
But how long can that last?

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:13.130
With a boost from Turquoise,

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.060
let's go!

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.670
I guard with Battle Sister, Chocolat!

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.640
I discard one card for perfect defense!

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.410
Perfect defense?

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.730
But, drive trigger...

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.070
First check...

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.310
Second check...

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:35.010
Skyhigh Walker.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:37.630
It's a stand trigger!

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.840
Stand, Alice!

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.340
And then I'll add +5000 to your power!

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.250
Even if I can protect against this attack, 
there'll be another one after it!

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:55.000
So... go on, Alice!

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.360
This time, make sure your attack 
on Amaterasu goes through!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.610
I guard with Chocolat!

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.720
I never thought she'd be able to 
pull off a perfect defense twice...

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.130
So this is as far as it goes...

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:28.400
Yes. This turn...

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:29.380
No.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:35.260
Asaka doesn't have a 
chance to attack anymore.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:41.810
Cerberus attacks Amaterasu 
with a boost from Bunny!

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.630
Tagitsuhime, Red Eye...

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:45.960
Intercept!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.130
Awesome!

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.940
She held out through four attacks!

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.040
Misaki!

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.420
That was great, girl!

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.900
GG, yo!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.330
It should be GM!

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.760
Wow...

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.490
You did it, Misaki!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:11.410
This is the first time anyone has made me 
bring down the curtain so humiliatingly.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:16.010
I acknowledge your ability, Misaki Tokura!

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:20.980
But that didn't do anything 
but buy you some time!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:25.240
After I make it through this 
next turn, you'll be finished!

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:29.980
Yes, that's true.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.870
<i>If</i> you make it through...

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.200
I stand and draw!

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.750
Just a little further...

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:48.320
What? What's she after?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.760
In our last fight,

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.160
your foresight was better than mine.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.610
But it's different this time.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.010
This field...

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:01.780
No, this <i>fight</i> is controlled by me!

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:09.690
Gentle light that illuminates the darkness...

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.830
Your smile will envelop the world...

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.380
I ride Goddess of the Full Moon...

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:16.590
Tsukuyomi!

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.510
Counterblast!

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:30.220
I draw two cards from my deck.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.970
I put one card from my hand into the Soul.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.390
And then, one more Counterblast!

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:41.960
I see...

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.590
This is what she was aiming for.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.340
I call Psychic Bird!

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.170
I activate its skill!

00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:58.460
I draw one card from my deck.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.070
I call one more Psychic Bird!

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:06.400
I activate its skill!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.090
And draw again...

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.320
I call Dark Cat!

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.320
I activate its skill!

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.700
When this unit enters the field,

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:24.390
if the Vanguard is an Oracle Think Tank unit,

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:27.030
both fighters may draw one card.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.080
I'm going to draw. How about you?

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:32.270
I'll draw.

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:44.360
I got it!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:50.830
I call Evil-eye Princess, Euryale!

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:56.340
Euryale's skill!

00:16:56.730 --> 00:17:00.290
I bind one card from your hand!

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:07.620
So you can't use that card during this turn.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.110
And then...

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.220
Call!

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.830
Beautiful Evil Eye Maiden, Euryale!

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.600
Seriously?!

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.060
That girl doesn't show any mercy!

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:23.570
Bind!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.820
I don't know what you're trying to do,

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:39.150
but for your three attacks this turn, I 
can still suffer 1 damage and be okay!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:44.270
Three attacks? Oh, no. All I need...

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.330
...is one!

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.510
With a boost from Goddess 
of the Crescent Moon,

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:54.200
attack Mistress Hurricane...

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.320
Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.610
18000 power...

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:05.240
I need to...

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:09.450
Candy Clown and Turquoise, 
protect the Vanguard!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:13.020
Drive trigger. First check...

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:20.490
Battle Sister, Ginger, and I give the extra 
critical to Goddess of the Full Moon!

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:23.050
Don't tell me you've...

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:24.730
Godhawk, Ichibyoshi,

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:29.040
Goddess of the Crescent Moon, Goddess 
of the Half Moon, and Amaterasu.

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:33.840
With their skills, I sent 16 
cards to the bottom of my deck.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:35.670
And this is...

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.200
...that first card!

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.960
This girl...

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:48.310
So she remembered all 16 cards?

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.760
In that short time?!

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.610
Second check...

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.950
This is also Battle Sister, Ginger.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.910
I give all of the effects 
to Goddess of the Full Moon.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.500
That's 28000 power!

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:06.740
Critical 3...!

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:21.950
I don't believe it...

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.070
Oracle Think Tank predicts the future.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.220
I told you, didn't I?

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:33.030
This fight is controlled by me.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:43.430
The winner: Misaki Tokura of Team Q4!

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.350
Yeah!!

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.160
Misaki did it!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.700
I knew she could!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.870
You've grown, Misaki.

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:56.980
Misaki!

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.540
You did it! You did it!

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:01.780
Nice fight!

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.470
That was incredible, Misaki!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.950
It's okay. You don't have to 
force yourself to praise me.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:08.230
It's not forced at all!

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:12.670
That's right! Nobody but you could've 
fought like that, Misaki!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.400
Thank you.

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:18.190
It's your turn next, Aichi.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:20.050
Right!

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.410
I've avenged myself.

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:37.720
Ren...

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.070
I wanted to be...

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:46.280
...Ren's number one fighter!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.180
Only for Ren...

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.970
You did well, Asaka.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.270
Ren!

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:05.090
Thanks to your loss, I'll 
be able to fight Aichi.

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:14.440
However, a loss is a loss.

00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:17.700
You're expelled from AL4.

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:19.970
Asaka...

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.680
You forgot this.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.250
Wait, Asaka.

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:41.080
What? It's in bad taste to 
look at a woman's tears.

00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:44.610
Why did you fight beside Ren?

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:47.350
You really are crude, aren't you?

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:50.190
I may want to see it...

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:51.630
See our leader...

00:21:51.630 --> 00:21:54.390
No... Ren... lose.

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:00.650
Instead of Kai, Aichi Sendou

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:04.690
could be the fighter that 
defeats Ren Suzugamori.

00:23:50.880 --> 00:23:52.840
Misaki, nice fight!

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:53.990
Next, it's my turn...

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:55.710
The time has finally come.

00:23:56.050 --> 00:24:00.000
The time to fight the decisive battle 
between two people who possess power.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.080
I'm not gonna use Psyqualia!

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:05.970
Like Kai, I'm gonna use 
my own skill to beat you!

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:09.020
Hmph. As long as it's not a boring fight...

00:24:09.430 --> 00:24:10.050
Ren...

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:13.150
Next time: Two Powers, Side-by-Side

00:24:13.150 --> 00:24:15.420
At this rate, I'll be no match for him!

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:18.860
I picture Psyqualia whispering 
for me to use it...
